Session 22: Embedded Database Setup (H2 Database)

What is an Embedded Database?
An Embedded Database is a database that runs inside your Spring Boot application.
It does not need to be installed separately like MySQL
When you start the Spring Boot application, the database starts automatically.
When the application stops, the database also stops (unless configured to save data).
Examples of Embedded Databases
H2 ✅ (Most Popular)
HSQLDB
Apache Derby
Spring Boot mostly uses H2.



Why do we use H2 Database?
Imagine you are learning Spring Boot.
If you use MySQL every time, you need to:
Install MySQL
Start MySQL Server
Create Database
Create Tables
Configure Username & Password



This takes time.
Instead, use H2.
It starts automatically.
So developers use H2 for:
Learning
Practice
Testing
Small Projects
Real Life Example


Suppose you are learning to drive a car.
You first practice in a simulator.
After learning, you drive a real car.
Similarly,
H2 = Practice Database
MySQL = Real Database



Advantages of H2

✅ Very Fast

✅ Lightweight

✅ No Installation Required

✅ Starts Automatically

✅ Good for Testing

✅ Easy Configuration

Disadvantages

❌ Data is temporary (by default)

❌ Not suitable for large applications

❌ Production applications use MySQL, Oracle, PostgreSQL, etc.




What is H2 Configuration?

Configuration means telling Spring Boot:
Which database to use
Database URL
Username
Password

This is done in application.properties.

Example:

spring.datasource.url=jdbc:h2:mem:testdb
spring.datasource.driverClassName=org.h2.Driver
spring.datasource.username=sa
spring.datasource.password=

spring.h2.console.enabled=true

spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update



What is Schema?

Schema means the structure of the database.
It includes:
Database
Tables
Columns
Data Types
Example


Employee Table

ID	Name	Salary
1	Rahul	50000

This table structure is called a Schema.


What is Schema Auto-Creation?

Normally we create tables manually.
Example:
CREATE TABLE Employee(
id INT,
name VARCHAR(30),
salary DOUBLE
);

But Spring Boot + Hibernate can create the table automatically.
This feature is called Schema Auto-Creation.


1. none

Spring does nothing.

2. create

Deletes old table and creates a new one every time.

3. create-drop

Creates tables when application starts.

Deletes them when application stops.

4. update ✅ (Most Used)

Keeps existing data.

Adds new columns if needed.


Interview Questions
1. What is H2 Database?
H2 is an embedded, lightweight, in-memory database used for development and testing.

2. Why do we use H2?
Because it requires no installation, starts automatically, and is easy to use for learning and testing.

3. What is Schema?
Schema is the structure of a database that contains tables, columns, and relationships.

4. What is ddl-auto=update?
It automatically creates or updates database tables based on the entity classes without deleting existing data.

5. Which database is generally used in production?
MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, or SQL Server are commonly used in production instead of H2.
