What is Cascade?

Cascade means:
"When the parent is affected, automatically affect the child too."
With Cascade:
Save Student
↓
Passport also saved automatically

Types of Cascade
1. ALL
Everything happens automatically.
Save
Update
Delete
Merge
Refresh
cascade = CascadeType.ALL

2. PERSIST
Only save child.
CascadeType.PERSIST
3. REMOVE
Delete child when parent is deleted.
CascadeType.REMOVE

Delete Student

↓

Delete Passport

4. MERGE
Updates child automatically.

5. REFRESH
Reload latest data from database.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Fetch Types
What is Fetch?
Fetch means
When should related data be loaded from the database?


There are two types.
1. EAGER Fetch
Loads parent and child immediately.


Example
Student student = repo.findById(1).get();
Database loads

Student
+
Passport
at the same time.
fetch = FetchType.EAGER


2. LAZY Fetch
Loads only the parent first.
Student only
Passport loads only when needed.
fetch = FetchType.LAZY

Example
Student
↓
Later
↓
Passport

This improves performance because unnecessary data is not loaded.

Difference Between EAGER and LAZY
Feature	     EAGER	                              LAZY
Data        loadedImmediately		               Only when accessed
Performance Can be slower if lots of related data	Usually faster and more efficient
Use when Related data is always required 	Related data is optional or large
